{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01NnV7VzhGp39grBUvotXREQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018EAFmb1kYYsAgJQ1wuDZsR","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Explore GKR fractional sumcheck code","subagent_type":"Explore","prompt":"I need to understand the GKR fractional sumcheck implementation in this CUDA backend. Please find and read the following files thoroughly:\n\n1. `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/fractional.rs` - Focus on:\n   - The `fractional_sumcheck_gpu` function signature and generic parameters\n   - The `observe_and_update` function (around lines 318-346)\n   - The main round loop (around line 655)\n   - The FoldEval path with `do_fused_sumcheck_round` calls\n   - The PrecomputeM path\n   - The `reconstruct_s_evals` function (around lines 1126-1163)\n\n2. `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/sponge.cu` - The GPU sponge implementation with DeviceSpongeState, sponge_observe, sponge_sample\n\n3. `crates/cuda-backend/src/sponge.rs` - The Rust side of DuplexSpongeGpu, especially sync_h2d\n\n4. `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/sumcheck.cu` - The existing CUDA sumcheck kernels, especially `frac_compute_round_and_fold` and `frac_compute_round_and_fold_inplace`\n\n5. `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/include/` - Available CUDA headers, especially fpext.h or any extension field headers\n\n6. `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs` - The caller of fractional_sumcheck_gpu\n\n7. `crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs` - FFI bindings for sumcheck kernels\n\nReport the key details: exact function signatures, line numbers, data types used, how DeviceBuffer works, how FFI is done, what FpExt/FracExt types look like in CUDA, etc. Be very thorough - I need all the details to implement changes."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8560,"cache_read_input_tokens":31063,"cache_cr