n\n### **2. Core Data Types**\n\n#### `Frac<EF>` (from openvm_stark_backend)\n- Imported from `openvm_stark_backend::prover::fractional_sumcheck_gkr::{Frac, FracSumcheckProof}`\n- In Rust: Generic pair type `(EF, EF)` representing numerator and denominator\n- In CUDA: `struct FracExt { FpExt p; FpExt q; }`\n- Size: 32 bytes (two FpExt = 2 × 16 bytes)\n- Memory layout: Binary-compatible between Rust and CUDA\n\n#### `EF` (Extension Field)\n```rust\n// From types.rs\npub use openvm_stark_sdk::config::baby_bear_poseidon2::{EF, ...};\n```\n- BabyBear extension field (F_p^4)\n- 128-bit field element (4 × 32-bit components)\n- Defined in CUDA as `struct FpExt` with `bb31_4_t` union for arithmetic\n\n#### `FpExt` CUDA Type (fpext.h)\n```c\nstruct FpExt {\n    union {\n        Fp elems[4];\n        bb31_4_t rep;  // Base field elements\n    };\n};\n```\n- Size: 16 bytes (static_assert at line 166)\n- Alignment: Same as `bb31_4_t`\n- Arithmetic via sppark's `bb31_4_t` implementation\n\n#### `DeviceBuffer<T>` (openvm_cuda_common)\n- RAII wrapper for GPU memory allocation\n- Methods:\n  - `with_capacity(size)`: Allocate capacity\n  - `as_ptr()`: Const raw pointer\n  - `as_mut_ptr()`: Mutable raw pointer  \n  - `as_raw_ptr()`: Raw pointer\n  - `is_empty()`: Check if allocated\n  - `len()`: Current size\n  - `to_host()`: Copy to host (returns Result<Vec<T>>)\n\n### **3. Main Round Loop (lines 655-1050)**\n\n**Loop Structure:**\n```rust\nfor round in 1..total_rounds {\n    // round == 1: first inner round (compute + revert fused)\n    // round == total_rounds-1: last outer round\n    \n    // Strategy selection (line 680):\n    backend = choose_round_strategy(\n        round,\n        precompute_m_env,        // SWIRL_CUDA_GKR_PRECOMPUTE_M\n        precompute_m_min_blocks_threshold,\n        precompute_m_target_blocks,\n        precompute_m_tail_tile_override,\n        precompute_m_min_n,\n    );\n```\n\n**Key Variables Managed:**\n- `pq_size`: Current layer size (starts at `2 <<