{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01WQux327X8eLvqPEMaSZ9nb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me analyze the results:\n\n**APC 300:**\n- Before: STARK excl trace = 1294ms, LogUp GKR = 527ms\n- After: STARK excl trace = 1305ms, LogUp GKR = 534ms\n- Change: STARK excl trace +11ms, LogUp GKR +7ms (no improvement, within noise)\n\n**APC 000:**\n- Before: STARK excl trace = 2153ms, LogUp GKR = 1034ms\n- After: STARK excl trace = 2165ms, LogUp GKR = 1041ms\n\n\n- Change: STARK excl trace +12ms, LogUp GKR +7ms (no improvement, within noise)\n\nThe optimization didn't help—I'm seeing a slight regression instead of the expected ~26ms improvement on LogUp GKR. The issue is likely that the postprocess kernel runs as a single-thread launch with ~5-10μs overhead per call, and replacing the D2H transfer with an on-device kernel isn't actually saving time since the kernel overhead and synchronization costs are eating up any gains.\n\nBut I'm realizing the baseline profiling data showing 14ms of inter-kernel gaps might be outdated—with the multistream and batch optimizations already in place, the fractional sumcheck probably has fewer rounds now, so the actual savings from eliminating those CPU-GPU transitions would be much smaller than originally estimated.\n\nLet me run the measurements again to rule out noise and see if there's actually any consistent improvement, or if this optimization just didn't move the needle.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1838,"cache_read_input_tokens":180707,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1838},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3d1d6996-d207-40ca-9042-54ec7bd5b430","uuid":"dee45ae2-0ea6-4c6c-b988-6f9d721d5144"}
